---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import FurtherReading from '../components/FurtherReading.astro';
import SeaBreak from '../components/SeaBreak.astro';
import { celestial, scenes } from '../config/images';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import CTABand from '../components/CTABand.astro';
const crumbs = [{ label: 'How Readings Work', href: '/how-readings-work/' }];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How Readings Work. What to expect"
  description="What happens in an astrology reading with Mo Lumen: booking, intake, preparation, the conversation itself, and what you take home."
  path="/how-readings-work/"
  breadcrumbs={crumbs}
>
  <Breadcrumbs crumbs={crumbs} />
  <section class="hero hero--split">
    <div class="container">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">What to expect</p>
        <h1>How readings work</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          You do not need to know astrology or know exactly what to say. I prepare the chart, guide
          the conversation, and make room for your questions and experience as we go.
        </p>
      </div>
      <img
        class="hero__img"
        src={scenes.readingProcess.src}
        srcset={scenes.readingProcess.srcset}
        sizes="100vw"
        alt={scenes.readingProcess.alt}
        width={scenes.readingProcess.width}
        height={scenes.readingProcess.height}
        fetchpriority="high"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose flow">
      <h2>Before we meet</h2>
      <p>
        When you book, you'll choose a time shown in your own time zone, pay securely online, and
        complete a short intake form with your birth details, what is bringing you in, and any
        questions you already know you want to ask. Then you'll receive preparation notes by email.
        They take only a few minutes to read, and there is nothing to study. Knowing the astrology
        is my responsibility, not yours.
      </p>
      <h2>Why I ask for your birth information</h2>
      <p>
        Your chart is calculated from your birth date, time, and place. Birth time gives us the
        ascendant and the chart's relationship to the local horizon and meridian, which is why it
        matters for houses and other time-sensitive techniques. The rising sign changes on average
        about every two hours, while the rising degree and many house cusps move continuously. A
        recorded birth time is therefore useful, but uncertainty does not make the rest of the chart
        disappear. If your time is unknown or uncertain, <a href="/birth-time/">the Birth Time guide
        explains what remains usable and what to do next</a>. We can shape the reading around what
        is solid. Your birth details are treated as sensitive personal information: they're used to
        prepare your reading and never sold, shared, or used for anything else. See the
        <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <SeaBreak image={celestial.lighthouse} />

  <section class="section section--sea">
    <div class="container prose flow">
      <h2>The session itself</h2>
      <p>
        We meet one-on-one over Zoom or phone (in person in DFW can sometimes be arranged). I will
        have studied your chart beforehand. From there, the reading becomes a conversation. I will
        explain what I see and why I am looking there, and I may ask how a possible pattern is
        showing up in your life. Your response helps me understand which of the chart's many
        possibilities is actually meaningful for you.
      </p>
      <p>
        You are welcome to ask questions and interrupt. You are also welcome to listen for a while
        before you know what you want to say. Some readings become very conversational quickly;
        others unfold more quietly. I will guide either one. The goal is not for you to perform as
        a client. It is for the astrology to become increasingly specific to the life you are living.
      </p>
      <h2>What you take home</h2>
      <p>
        Every live session includes a recording and a copy of your chart. A second listen can be
        useful because it gives you time to hear the conversation again without also having to take
        it in for the first time.
      </p>
      <h2>What readings are, and aren't</h2>
      <p>
        Most readings are about perspective, pattern recognition, and timing rather than telling
        you what decision to make. Some branches of astrology, including horary, are designed to
        answer a specific question more directly; when I use those methods, I will be clear about
        what the technique supports and what it does not. Astrology is not medical, psychological,
        legal, or financial advice, and if your question belongs with one of those professionals,
        I'll say so plainly. See the <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a> for the full picture.
      </p>
      <p>
        Readings can also be given as a gift. See <a href="/readings/gift/">gift readings</a> for
        how that works.
      </p>
      <FurtherReading />
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTABand
    heading="Bring what is actually on your mind."
    body="You do not need to prepare the perfect question or know the astrology. I will bring the chart and the preparation; we will take it from there together."
  />
</BaseLayout>
